<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A5.7's watchdog, and the reason it lives HERE and not in the .252 crontab: it must fail
  independently of the thing it watches. The reporter runs on 192.168.100.252 at 21:00 ET; a box that
  is down reports nothing AND fails to notice that nothing was reported. This runs on the dev Mac at
  07:00 ET, checking the PREVIOUS trading day, so the two cannot go quiet together.

  Install: run scripts/ops/archive/install-dev-mac-watchdog.sh. Do NOT copy files by hand.

  These instructions used to list the copies to make, and they went stale the moment the watchdog
  gained another file to read: they named the script and oe-alert.sh but not calibration-targets.env
  or oe_corpus_reader.py, so following them installed a watchdog that refuses to run on its first
  wake-up (r23 #1). The installer owns that list, installs every file the script reads from beside
  itself, RUNS it once to prove it starts — RunAtLoad is false, so loading the agent proves nothing —
  and fails unless exactly one agent registers.

      bash scripts/ops/archive/install-dev-mac-watchdog.sh

  Pass the dry-run flag first to see what it would write without writing it. (A literal double dash
  cannot appear inside an XML comment, which is why the flag is spelled out rather than shown.)

  scripts/ci/validate-dev-mac-watchdog.sh checks that this file and that installer still agree.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.optionsedge.calibration-progress-watch</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/calibration-progress-watch.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>ENV</key><string>prod</string>
    <!--
      ARCHIVE_DIR is deliberately NOT set here. It used to say /Volumes/database/optionsedge, which is
      not where the NAS is mounted on this Mac (//192.168.100.100/database is on $HOME/nas-db), so this
      agent would have alerted MISSING every trading day forever and been ignored within a week
      (BZ 360). The script resolves the root from ARCHIVE_ROOT_CANDIDATES instead, and if it finds
      none it says "this is a MOUNT problem here" rather than blaming the reporter on .252.
      Set it here only to override that on a host where the candidates are wrong.
    -->
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/calibration-progress-watch.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/calibration-progress-watch.err.log</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
</dict>
</plist>
